From: rknpu-rk3588 project <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] gem: fix the non-contiguous fallback of contiguous allocations with the IOMMU

When a RKNPU_MEM_CONTIGUOUS allocation fails with the IOMMU enabled
(typically larger than what is left in CMA), rknpu_gem_alloc_buf()
falls back to a non-contiguous buffer: it sets RKNPU_MEM_NON_CONTIGUOUS
but still allocates it with dma_alloc_attrs(). With the IOMMU, objects
flagged RKNPU_MEM_NON_CONTIGUOUS are mmapped and freed through the
shmem page path (rknpu_gem_mmap_pages(), rknpu_gem_put_pages()), so the
fallback object is inconsistent:

  RKNPU: try to fallback to allocate non-contiguous 268435456 buffer.
  RKNPU: failed to map pages into vma: -6
  refcount_t: underflow; use-after-free.
  WARNING: lib/refcount.c:28 at refcount_warn_saturate+0xf4/0x148

Use rknpu_gem_get_pages() for the fallback too, after freeing the page
array allocated for the contiguous attempt. Also pass __GFP_NOWARN to
the contiguous attempt when the IOMMU is enabled: its failure is
expected and handled, and otherwise triggers a page allocator warning
for the huge order.

Tested on Radxa ROCK 5B (RK3588), Armbian 7.3.4-edge-rockchip64, CMA
256 MB: 256 MB + 512 MB + 1 GB contiguous requests are served through
the fallback, mapped, written and read back, without any warning.

--- a/src/rknpu_gem.c
+++ b/src/rknpu_gem.c
@@ -191,6 +191,15 @@
 	if (rknpu_obj->flags & RKNPU_MEM_ZEROING)
 		gfp_mask |= __GFP_ZERO;
 
+	/*
+	 * With the IOMMU, a failed physically contiguous allocation is
+	 * expected (CMA too small) and handled by the fallback below; do not
+	 * let the page allocator warn about the huge order.
+	 */
+	if (rknpu_dev->iommu_en &&
+	    !(rknpu_obj->flags & RKNPU_MEM_NON_CONTIGUOUS))
+		gfp_mask |= __GFP_NOWARN;
+
 	if (!rknpu_dev->iommu_en ||
 	    rknpu_dev->config->dma_mask <= DMA_BIT_MASK(32) ||
 	    (rknpu_obj->flags & RKNPU_MEM_DMA32)) {
@@ -222,6 +231,20 @@
 				rknpu_obj->size);
 			rknpu_obj->dma_attrs &= ~DMA_ATTR_FORCE_CONTIGUOUS;
 			rknpu_obj->flags |= RKNPU_MEM_NON_CONTIGUOUS;
+#if RKNPU_GEM_ALLOC_FROM_PAGES
+			/*
+			 * With the IOMMU, RKNPU_MEM_NON_CONTIGUOUS objects
+			 * are mmapped and freed through the shmem page path
+			 * (rknpu_gem_mmap_pages(), rknpu_gem_put_pages()).
+			 * Allocating the fallback with dma_alloc_attrs() made
+			 * mmap fail (-ENXIO) and the free path put pages it did
+			 * not own (refcount underflow, use-after-free). Use the
+			 * page path for the fallback too.
+			 */
+			rknpu_gem_free_page(rknpu_obj->pages);
+			rknpu_obj->pages = NULL;
+			return rknpu_gem_get_pages(rknpu_obj);
+#endif
 			rknpu_obj->cookie = dma_alloc_attrs(
 				drm->dev, rknpu_obj->size, &rknpu_obj->dma_addr,
 				gfp_mask, rknpu_obj->dma_attrs);
